_LITERAL | NAME_LITERAL\nlist_lit ::= \"[\" value (\",\" value)* \"]\"\ndiff ::= HANDLE \"-\" NUMBER_LITERAL\nproposition ::= intent_symbol \"(\" proposition_arg_list? \")\"\nproposition_arg_list ::= proposition_arg (\",\" proposition_arg)*\nproposition_arg ::= attribute_symbol \"=\" value\nontology_symbol ::= operation_symbol | entity_symbol | role_symbol | intent_symbol | attribute_value_symbol\nHANDLE ::= \"$\" [a-z] [a-z0-9_]*\nNUMBER_LITERAL ::= \"-\"? [0-9]+ (\".\" [0-9]+)?\nDATE_LITERAL ::= \"@d\" [0-9]{4} \"-\" [0-9]{2} \"-\" [0-9]{2}\nTIME_LITERAL ::= \"@t\" [0-9]{2} \":\" [0-9]{2} \":\" [0-9]{2} \"Z\"\nURL_LITERAL ::= \"@u\" [a-z0-9._~:/?#\\[\\]@!$&'()*+,;=%-]+\nPATH_LITERAL ::= \"@p\" [a-zA-Z0-9._/-]+\nNAME_LITERAL ::= \"@n\" [a-zA-Z0-9_-]+\n-- All uppercase keywords, operators, punctuation delimiters, type names, and lexical forms are members of structural-symbol; all non-structural source symbols must match exactly one glossary vocabulary category.", "semantics": "BrainCode source has no STRING type and no quoted-text literal. NUMBER, BOOL, DATE, TIME, URL, PATH, NAME, LIST[T], REF[T], and PROPOSITION are the only value types. DATE, TIME, URL, PATH, and NAME literals are atomic lexical values defined by literal-form; their internal characters are not interpreted as natural-language syntax. HANDLE is an opaque local reference created only by a binding, parameter, task declaration, turn declaration, or loop declaration; its spelling carries no descriptive meaning. An ontology symbol is valid only if the glossary category that admits it defines its meaning and type. A proposition is a symbolic intent with glossary-defined, canonically ordered attributes. Every proposition attribute must be permitted for that intent by the intent-symbol entry, and its value must belong to that attribute's glossary-defined value set or be a type permitted by that attribute.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Ask the manager for a two-day extension politely.", "braincode": "intent_request_extension(recipient=role_manager, duration=2, unit=value_day, tone=value_polite)"}, "glossary_gloss": "Types & Lexicon defines every legal kind of BrainCode value and every rule for producing a source token. It forbids quoted prose and makes symbolic propositions the way requests and message meaning are represented.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "The former STRING and IDENT productions admitted arbitrary English phrases and arbitrary descriptive names, which made expressions impossible to trace completely through the glossary. This revision supplies a closed lexical basis, while retaining open-ended atomic data only through exact literal rules.", "cites_source": "Formal language theory (general)", "addresses_note": "N1"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "structural-symbol", "glossary_gloss": "Structural symbols are BrainCode's reserved keywords, operators, type names, and delimiters. They describe syntax rather than a requested-world concept.", "closed": true, "members": [{"symbol": "ENTRYPOINT", "gloss": "Declares the one execution root of a document.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "TASK", "gloss": "Begins a task declaration.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "ACTION", "gloss": "Begins an external operation.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "UTTER", "gloss": "Begins a non-effectful speech act.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "GENERATE", "gloss": "Begins a non-effectful symbolic artifact generation step.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "CONVO", "gloss": "Begins a conversation declaration.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "TURN", "gloss": "Begins a conversation turn.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "IF", "gloss": "Begins a conditional branch.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "THEN", "gloss": "Begins the true branch of a conditional.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "ELSE", "gloss": "Begins the false branch of a conditional.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "FOR", "gloss": "Begins iteration.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "E