  "note_argument": "Every source token is now either a member of structural-symbol, admitted by an exact glossary-defined lexical rule, or a member of a disjoint ontology category with a defined schema. Quoted prose and unrestricted identifiers are prohibited; message content, operations, attributes, code evidence, dates, bindings, and control syntax are represented by glossary-defined symbolic forms.",
  "foundations_overview": "BrainCode is a closed-vocabulary, statically typed context-free language whose source alphabet is completely defined by its glossary. Structural syntax is finite and explicitly glossary-listed; open-ended data may occur only through exact atomic literal forms. Descriptive meaning is represented by disjoint, glossary-governed ontology categories and recursively typed propositions, never by natural-language fragments. Local references use canonically allocated opaque handles, while actions, utterances, generation requests, code evidence, control flow, and conversation revisions all compose through fixed schemas and canonical ordering rules.",
