      "construct_name": "Types & Lexicon",
      "grammar": "type ::= NUMBER | BOOL | DATE | TIME | URL | PATH | NAME | CODE | PROPOSITION | ENTITY | ROLE | VALUE | LIST \"[\" type \"]\" | REF \"[\" type \"]\"\nvalue ::= literal | entity_symbol | role_symbol | value_symbol | HANDLE | list_lit | proposition | code | diff\nliteral ::= NUMBER_LITERAL | TRUE | FALSE | DATE_LITERAL | TIME_LITERAL | URL_LITERAL | PATH_LITERAL | NAME_LITERAL\nlist_lit ::= \"[\" value (\",\" value)* \"]\"\ndiff ::= HANDLE \"-\" NUMBER_LITERAL\nproposition ::= intent_symbol \"(\" proposition_arg_list? \")\"\nproposition_arg_list ::= proposition_arg (\",\" proposition_arg)*\nproposition_arg ::= attribute_symbol \"=\" value\ncode ::= code_node\nontology_symbol ::= operation_symbol | intent_symbol | entity_symbol | role_symbol | value_symbol | attribute_symbol\nHANDLE ::= \"$v\" POSITIVE_INTEGER\nNUMBER_LITERAL ::= \"-\"? (\"0\" | [1-9][0-9]*) ( \".\" [0-9]+ )?\nDATE_LITERAL ::= \"@d\" YYYY \"-\" MM \"-\" DD\nTIME_LITERAL ::= \"@t\" HH \":\" MM \":\" SS \"Z\"\nURL_LITERAL ::= \"@u\" URL_BODY\nPATH_LITERAL ::= \"@p\" PATH_BODY\nNAME_LITERAL ::= \"@n\" NAME_BODY\n-- Ontology categories are namespace-disjoint: operation symbols begin op_; intent symbols begin int_; entity symbols begin ent_; role symbols begin role_; value symbols begin val_; attribute symbols begin attr_.",
      "semantics": "BrainCode has no STRING type and no quoted-text syntax. Every ontology symbol has one category-defined static type: entity_symbol has ENTITY, role_symbol has ROLE, value_symbol has VALUE, proposition has PROPOSITION, and CODE has CODE. operation_symbol, intent_symbol, and attribute_symbol are syntactic-position symbols only: an operation may occur only after ACTION, an intent only as a proposition head or after UTTER, and an attribute only as a schema-authorized argument label. They are never general values. DATE_LITERAL must be a valid proleptic-Gregorian calendar date. TIME_LITERAL is UTC and requires 00-23 hours, 00-59 minutes, and 00-59 seconds. URL_LITERAL is an RFC-3986 absolute URI serialized without whitespace or quotation marks. PATH_LITERAL is an absolute or relative slash-normalized path with no whitespace, dot-segment, repeated-slash, or backslash form. NAME_LITERAL is a single atomic proper-name token using NFC Unicode letters, decimal digits, underscore, or hyphen only, beginning with a letter; casing is preserved and has no grammatical meaning. Literal productions are mutually exclusive by their required prefixes. HANDLE allocation is mandatory and canonical: traverse the finalized document preorder, assigning $v1 to the ENTRYPOINT target, then each declaration name, parameter, result binding, turn name, loop binding, and LET binding at its first introduction in source order; a later reference must use its allocated handle. A handle suffix has no meaning.",
