   "membership_rule": "CODE grammar is: code_node ::= code_call(callee=CODE,args=LIST[CODE]) | code_assign(target=CODE,value=CODE) | code_list(items=LIST[CODE]) | code_map(entries=LIST[CODE]) | code_command(tokens=LIST[CODE]) | code_assert(expected=CODE,actual=CODE) | code_tokens(tokens=LIST[CODE]) | code_id | code_text | NUMBER_LITERAL. @i and @q are atomic hexadecimal encodings, never natural-language syntax. A code tree is ordered, typed, and exact; its decoded codepoint sequence is data, not BrainCode prose.",
